WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.924
A roster, a neighbour notice and a record
summary have different checks.

2
00:00:05.924 --> 00:00:10.804
AI can prepare a draft from the notes you
give it.

3
00:00:10.804 --> 00:00:16.571
The farmer still checks the assignments,
dates and status before anyone uses it.

4
00:00:16.571 --> 00:00:20.120
Our Example Station material is invented
for practice.

5
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.332
Worker A is available Monday and Tuesday.

6
00:00:24.332 --> 00:00:27.744
Worker B is available Tuesday and
Wednesday.

7
00:00:27.744 --> 00:00:30.181
Each morning needs one check.

8
00:00:30.181 --> 00:00:34.568
A draft putting A on Wednesday breaks the
note.

9
00:00:34.568 --> 00:00:41.393
If B also becomes unavailable, Wednesday
needs a visible gap for the manager to

10
00:00:41.393 --> 00:00:41.880
resolve.

11
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:48.610
For a proposed neighbour spray notice,
exact timing, hazards, affected people

12
00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.305
and notification arrangements need
confirmation.

13
00:00:51.305 --> 00:00:55.617
Ask for a preparation draft with visible
gaps.

14
00:00:55.617 --> 00:01:01.547
The responsible operator checks the label,
applicable regional plan and GROWSAFE

15
00:01:01.547 --> 00:01:02.086
guidance.

16
00:01:02.086 --> 00:01:05.320
A notice cannot approve the job.

17
00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.842
A contractor email should ask whether a
day suits when no booking is agreed.

18
00:01:11.842 --> 00:01:15.929
Check recipients and attachments before a
real message is sent.

19
00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:20.424
A vet enquiry should keep observations
separate from diagnosis and treatment,

20
00:01:20.424 --> 00:01:24.920
with urgent concerns taken directly to the
vet under farm arrangements.

21
00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.938
For records, preserve the original status.

22
00:01:28.938 --> 00:01:32.693
Maintenance planned must not become
maintenance completed.

23
00:01:32.693 --> 00:01:37.520
An activity log does not prove an
inspection happened.

24
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:43.956
A useful compliance draft lists the
source, the missing evidence and the

25
00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:45.565
person to ask.

26
00:01:45.565 --> 00:01:49.320
Keep the original record beside the draft.

27
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:55.670
In the activity, assemble a prompt from
the supplied chips and watch the sample

28
00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:56.463
draft change.

29
00:01:56.463 --> 00:01:59.238
Then review the missing dates and hazards.

30
00:01:59.238 --> 00:02:00.428
Nothing is sent.

31
00:02:00.428 --> 00:02:06.374
Use the same source check on any roster,
notice or email you prepare later, and

32
00:02:06.374 --> 00:02:07.960
keep unresolved questions visible.
